#align(center)[#v(3em) #text(18pt, font: "Cinzel", weight: "bold")[Chapter 1]]
#align(center)[#text(12pt, style: "italic")[The Embers of Mount Ignis]]
#v(2em)
#align(right)[#text(9pt, font: "Cinzel", fill: luma(90))[POV: Lord Raymond Vael]]
#v(1em)
The frost gathered on the ramparts of the [[Citadel_of_Ash]] like spilled salt. Below in the caldera, the great geothermal hearth pulsed with a low, rhythmic heartbeat that vibrated through Raymond's boots.

Raymond adjusted his heavy mantle of wolfskin, his violet eyes narrowing as he gazed out over the jagged obsidian spires of the Ashmarch. The scouts had returned before dawn, their horses lathered and trembling. The vanguard of the [[Solar_Ascendancy]] was marching along the Sunstone Pass, banners of mirrored gold blazing in the morning light.

"They bring twelve battalions, my Lord," muttered Captain Bran, breath misting in the cold air.

Raymond reached down and touched the basalt parapet. With a focused breath, he drew upon the [[Investiture_of_Cinders]]. Heat flowed from the stone into his marrow, cooling the surrounding stone to a brittle ice while filling his veins with kinetic fire.

"Let them bring fifty," Raymond said softly. "The caldera yields to no emperor."

#v(1.5em)

The great doors of the Obsidian Throne Room swung inward with a groan of iron. [[Lady_Aurelia_Sol]] stepped onto the polished black floor, the hem of her sun-silk robes whispering against the flagstones.

She paused, taking in the cavernous hall. Above, soot-stained banners of [[House_Vael]] hung from vaulted ribs of basalt. At the dais sat Raymond Vael, his silver hair catching the amber glow of the hearth braziers.

"Lord Warden," Aurelia began, inclining her head just enough to satisfy diplomatic courtesy without ceding imperial dignity. Her golden eyes swept over the council of captains. "The Solar Ascendancy offers terms of eternal alliance. Grant us access to the lower ember-forges, and the Emperor will guarantee the sovereignty of the Ashmarch for three centuries."

Raymond leaned forward, resting his chin on his steepled fingers. "And if we refuse to surrender the ancient hearth of Mount Ignis?"

Aurelia smiled thinly. "The sun rises over all lands, Lord Vael. Even those buried under ash."

#v(1.5em)

#pagebreak()
#align(center)[#v(3em) #text(18pt, font: "Cinzel", weight: "bold")[Chapter 2]]
#align(center)[#text(12pt, style: "italic")[The Siege of the Red Pass]]
#v(2em)
#align(right)[#text(9pt, font: "Cinzel", fill: luma(90))[POV: Lord Raymond Vael]]
#v(1em)
Dawn broke over Sunstone Pass in shards of crimson and fractured gold.

Raymond stood atop the narrow defile where the mountain road squeezed between two shearing cliffs of basalt. Below in the canyon, the imperial legion advanced in disciplined testudo formations, their mirrored shields deflecting the morning fog.

"Hold the line until they enter the funnel!" Raymond commanded.

He extended his hands, palms downward toward the volcanic fissure beneath his boots. The magma subterranean veins surged in response. Drawing deep on the [[Investiture_of_Cinders]], Raymond felt the bitter chill of thermodynamic transfer freeze the sweat upon his brow as raw volcanic heat coiled like a serpent within his chest.

With a sharp release, he drove the stored kinetic energy straight into the bedrock.

A deafening crack tore through the canyon. The forward ridge collapsed in an avalanche of shattered stone, cutting off the imperial vanguard from their supply train in a single stroke.

#v(1.5em)
